[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: No node outside the representation family may carry a Parent relation to a narrative

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-NOTHING-DEPENDS-ON-A-NARRATIVE
TITLE: No node outside the representation family may carry a Parent relation to a narrative
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A narrative presents; it is never presented. No REQUIREMENT, DECISION,
MECHANISM, EVIDENCE, USE_CASE or WORK may carry a Parent relation -- of any
role -- or a PARENT_FP entry to a NARRATIVE. A narrative may Cites anything
and Contains only narratives. This keeps every narrative a pure sink:
outside every readiness closure, never signed against, never able to close
a cycle, and collectable with its plan without stranding a fingerprint.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The grammar cannot say it -- roles are registered on the source, and the target's type is never checked -- so it is a rule for the relation-target lint when that is built and for the view check until then.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Nothing enforces this yet; MECH-VIEW-CHECK covers it for narratives in the trees it walks, and MECH-RELATION-TARGET-TYPE-LINT would cover the corpus.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-NARRATIVE-IS-THE-VIEW-NODE
  ROLE: Governed_By
